<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Minimal-RL Training Details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We mainly follow the Minimal-RL recipe <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2025</a>)</cite> in our experiments to ensure a fair comparison among different rollout sampling strategies. Specifically, we set a series of hyperparameters as in <a href="#A1.T1" title="In Appendix A Minimal-RL Training Details ‣ Let it Calm: Exploratory Annealed Decoding for Verifiable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Hyperparameter</th>
<th id="A1.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Value(s)</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Training Batch Size</td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1024</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Max Prompt Length</td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1024</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Max Response Length</td>
<td id="A1.T1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3072</td></tr>
