<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Off-policy Issue and Truncated Importance Sampling Correction</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Sampling Techniques Can Introduce Off-Policy Issue</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One subtle yet troublesome drawback of reinforcement learning with sampling techniques is that it simultaneously introduces the <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">off-policy</em> problem: there is a gap between the behavior policy (used for sampling) and the target policy (being optimized and parametrized by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>). This might introduce instability to the training and cause it to fail (See example training of RLVR with EAD <a href="#A2.F11" title="In B.1 Sampling Techniques Can Introduce Off-Policy Issue ‣ Appendix B Off-policy Issue and Truncated Importance Sampling Correction ‣ Let it Calm: Exploratory Annealed Decoding for Verifiable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05251v1/pg_clipfrac_Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B.svg" id="A2.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/403;" width="548" height="403"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Clip Fraction Surge</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05251v1/grad_norm_Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B.svg" id="A2.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/375;" width="548" height="375"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Gradient Norm Surge.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A2.F11.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05251v1/best_at_16_Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B.svg" id="A2.F11.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/389;" width="548" height="389"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Drastic Best@16 Drop</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A2.F11.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05251v1/legend-fig3.svg" id="A2.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/377;" width="548" height="377"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Off-policy samples bring training instability. The base model is Qwen2.5-Math-1.5B.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Noted that this off-policy phenomenon widely exists for any efficient sampling framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and sampling strategy (for instance, when applying best-of-<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2025</a>)</cite> or filtering out responses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shrivastava et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, the underlying distribution of responses is implicitly altered). To be more precise, we take the policy gradient loss as an example:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\frac{\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}}\times\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sampling</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sampling</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\frac{\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}}\times\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mtext>sampling</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the underlying sampling distribution.
In such case, an extra weight is implicitly added to each response in addition to its advantage <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(y;x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(y;x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This extra weight can significantly inflate the variance of the policy gradient, posing a stability challenge that our proposed EAD needs to mitigate.
To quantify this effect in our proposed EAD, we now analyze such variance under a standard, fixed <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">temperature sampling</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math> to define a policy <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the effect of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on the variance of the gradient estimator. We reduce the problem to analyzing the variance inflation factor</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x;\tau)}\left[\frac{\pi(y\mid x;1)^{2}}{\pi(y\mid x;\tau)^{2}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x;\tau)}\left[\frac{\pi(y\mid x;1)^{2}}{\pi(y\mid x;\tau)^{2}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We begin with one-token case. Let <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th token in the vocabulary <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is its logit. Then equation <a href="#A2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ B.1 Sampling Techniques Can Introduce Off-Policy Issue ‣ Appendix B Off-policy Issue and Truncated Importance Sampling Correction ‣ Let it Calm: Exploratory Annealed Decoding for Verifiable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> can be rewritten as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}\frac{h_{i}/(\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h_{j})}{h^{1/\tau}_{i}/(\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{j})}\times\frac{h_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h_{j}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-1/\tau}\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{i}}{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}\right)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}\frac{h_{i}/(\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h_{j})}{h^{1/\tau}_{i}/(\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{j})}\times\frac{h_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{|V|}h_{j}}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-1/\tau}\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{i}}{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}\right)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in V</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-1/\tau}\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-1/\tau}\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{1/\tau}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing when <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and increasing when <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies it has a global minimum at <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=1/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=1/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. We define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}\right)+\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{x}_{i}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}\right)+\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h^{x}_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Its derivative is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)=\frac{-\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}}+\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)=\frac{-\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{2-x}}+\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">To analyze the sign of <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define a helper function <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)</annotation></semantics></math> and its sign depends on whether <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than, less than, or equal to <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(2-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(2-x)</annotation></semantics></math>. We take a look at derivative of <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(x)=\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}(\log h_{i})^{2}\right)\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\right)-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}\right)^{2}}{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\right)^{2}}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(x)=\frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}(\log h_{i})^{2}\right)\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\right)-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\log h_{i}\right)^{2}}{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{|V|}h_{i}^{x}\right)^{2}}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is an increasing function and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)\geq 0,~~\mathrm{when}~x\geq 1\\
~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)=0,~~\mathrm{when}~x=1\\
~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)\leq 0,~~\mathrm{when}~x\leq 1.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>when</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>when</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi>when</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)\geq 0,~~\mathrm{when}~x\geq 1\\
~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)=0,~~\mathrm{when}~x=1\\
~f^{\prime}(x)=g(x)-g(2-x)\leq 0,~~\mathrm{when}~x\leq 1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Accordingly, <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing when <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and is decreasing when <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the proposition easily follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The same conclusion can be proved for multiple-token sequence by induction. Therefore, we get that
when the temperature is far from 1, the off-policy issue could be severe and lead to large variance of the gradient estimator.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Truncated Importance Sampling Ratio Correction</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To cancel such bias, an importance sampling ratio can be introduced <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hilton et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}}\times\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sampling</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">old</mtext></msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sampling</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}\mathbin{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi^{\text{sampling}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}}\times\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To further prevent negative effects by the extreme likelihood ratios and boost training stability, we truncate the likelihood ratio with an upper bound. That is, <em id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">truncated importance sampling</em> technique <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heckman et al., 1998</a>)</cite>. Taking the vanilla policy gradient loss as an example, the modified loss for EAD is as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}{\pi^{\text{EAD}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\min\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi^{\text{EAD}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)},\varepsilon\right)}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>EAD</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">min</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">π</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">θ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">old</mtext></msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">EAD</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y{\sim}{\pi^{\text{EAD}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid x)}}\left[{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\min\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}{\pi^{\text{EAD}}_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)},\varepsilon\right)}\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y\mid x)}A(y;x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Temperature-Entropy Relationship</h2>

<div id="A3.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The entropy of the softmax distribution is a non-decreasing function of the temperature <math id="A3.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The strategy is to show that the entropy <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-increasing function of the inverse temperature <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The probability of sampling token <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with temperature <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the policy <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity in the derivation, we denote this probability as <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}(\tau)\triangleq\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}=v\mid[x,y_{&lt;t}];\tau)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}(\tau)\triangleq\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}=v\mid[x,y_{&lt;t}];\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> be the logit for a token <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in the vocabulary <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability of a token as a function of <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{v}(\beta)=\frac{\exp(\beta h_{v})}{\sum_{v^{\prime}\in V}\exp(\beta h_{v^{\prime}})}\triangleq\frac{\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{v}(\beta)=\frac{\exp(\beta h_{v})}{\sum_{v^{\prime}\in V}\exp(\beta h_{v^{\prime}})}\triangleq\frac{\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function. The entropy, as a function of <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(\beta)=-\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)\log p_{v}(\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\beta)=-\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)\log p_{v}(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can rewrite the entropy by substituting <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{v}(\beta)=\beta h_{v}-\log Z(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{v}(\beta)=\beta h_{v}-\log Z(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)(\beta h_{v}-\log Z(\beta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)(\beta h_{v}-\log Z(\beta))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log Z(\beta)\left(\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)\right)-\beta\sum_{v\in V}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log Z(\beta)\left(\sum_{v\in V}p_{v}(\beta)\right)-\beta\sum_{v\in V}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log Z(\beta)-\beta\cdot\mathbb{E}_{v\sim p(\beta)}[h_{v}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log Z(\beta)-\beta\cdot\mathbb{E}_{v\sim p(\beta)}[h_{v}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we differentiate <math id="A3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{h}(\beta)=\mathbb{E}[h_{v}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{h}(\beta)=\mathbb{E}[h_{v}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\frac{d}{d\beta}(\log Z(\beta))-\frac{d}{d\beta}(\beta\bar{h}(\beta))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\frac{d}{d\beta}(\log Z(\beta))-\frac{d}{d\beta}(\beta\bar{h}(\beta)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">First, we find the derivative of the log-partition function:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\beta}(\log Z(\beta))=\frac{Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)}=\frac{\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)}=\sum_{v}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)=\bar{h}(\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\beta}(\log Z(\beta))=\frac{Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)}=\frac{\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)}=\sum_{v}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)=\bar{h}(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we use the product rule for the second term:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\beta}(\beta\bar{h}(\beta))=\bar{h}(\beta)+\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\beta}(\beta\bar{h}(\beta))=\bar{h}(\beta)+\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these gives:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\bar{h}(\beta)-\left(\bar{h}(\beta)+\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}\right)=-\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\bar{h}(\beta)-\left(\bar{h}(\beta)+\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}\right)=-\beta\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">The derivative <math id="A3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the variance of the logits. We can show this by differentiating <math id="A3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{h}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{h}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\bar{h}}{d\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{d}{d\beta}\left(\frac{\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{d}{d\beta}\left(\frac{\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v})}{Z(\beta)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(\sum_{v}h_{v}^{2}\exp(\beta h_{v}))Z(\beta)-(\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v}))Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(\sum_{v}h_{v}^{2}\exp(\beta h_{v}))Z(\beta)-(\sum_{v}h_{v}\exp(\beta h_{v}))Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{v}h_{v}^{2}p_{v}(\beta)-\left(\sum_{v}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)\right)\left(\frac{Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>v</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{v}h_{v}^{2}p_{v}(\beta)-\left(\sum_{v}h_{v}p_{v}(\beta)\right)\left(\frac{Z^{\prime}(\beta)}{Z(\beta)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[h^{2}]-(\mathbb{E}[h])^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{v\sim p(\beta)}(h_{v})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[h^{2}]-(\mathbb{E}[h])^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{v\sim p(\beta)}(h_{v}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back, we arrive at the final expression for the derivative of entropy:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\beta}=-\beta\cdot\mathrm{Var}_{v\sim p(\beta)}(h_{v})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\beta}=-\beta\cdot\mathrm{Var}_{v\sim p(\beta)}(h_{v}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the temperature <math id="A3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the inverse temperature <math id="A3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The variance of any random variable is non-negative. This can be formally shown using <span id="A3.p2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Jensen’s inequality</span>: for the convex function <math id="A3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi(h)]\geq\phi(\mathbb{E}[h])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi(h)]\geq\phi(\mathbb{E}[h])</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h^{2}]\geq(\mathbb{E}[h])^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h^{2}]\geq(\mathbb{E}[h])^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(h)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(h)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the derivative of entropy with respect to <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is non-positive:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\underbrace{-\beta}_{\leq 0}\cdot\underbrace{\mathrm{Var}(h_{v})}_{\geq 0}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dH}{d\beta}=\underbrace{-\beta}_{\leq 0}\cdot\underbrace{\mathrm{Var}(h_{v})}_{\geq 0}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-increasing function of <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is inversely proportional to <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> must be a non-decreasing function of the temperature <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Increasing Length in RL Training</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During RL training, our algorithm (EAD) incentivizes the model to generate longer, more effective reasoning chains for difficult problems, especially for 7B models (<a href="#A4.F12" title="In Appendix D Increasing Length in RL Training ‣ Let it Calm: Exploratory Annealed Decoding for Verifiable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). While both EAD and temperature sampling initially learn to shorten their responses by shifting from complex code-based solutions to direct mathematical reasoning, their behavior later diverges. The response length from temperature sampling stabilizes, whereas EAD learns to selectively increase reasoning length for harder problems, which boosts final performance. For these experiments, EAD is applied in the DAPO algorithm for sampling rollouts. We use the same training setup as detailed in <a href="#S5" title="5 Experiments ‣ Let it Calm: Exploratory Annealed Decoding for Verifiable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.05251v1/response-length.svg" id="A4.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/206;" width="548" height="206"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Compared with normal temperature sampling, EAD can naturally incentivize the model to generate longer reasoning chains. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
